abstract: >-
  LaTeX source, reproduction scripts, Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization (616 compared theorems, accepted by
  Comparator with the Lean and NanoDa kernels), leanblueprint and interactive explainers of the manuscript
  "Low-discrepancy quasi-uniform digital nets in every dimension" (version 1), which constructs, for every
  dimension s >= 3, explicit low-discrepancy digital nets in a fixed base whose minimum distance and covering
  radius are of the optimal order N^(-1/s), answering a question of Dick, Goda and Suzuki. The constructions,
  proofs and Lean formalization were produced by AI systems under the author's direction; see the section
  "Use of AI" of README.md.
